        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> ** based on a true story.. with some imagination added in here and there to keep you from falling asleep **</P><P>The Great War of Oasis<BR>----------------------<BR>	One afternoon, as many adventurers stood upon the swaying wooden dock in Oasis, a distant bellow of rage could be heard far off in the distance, beyond the dunes. Within moments, a small figure could be seen streaking across the dunes, headed for the gathering at the water's edge. Few regarded him as he wearily clawed his way into the confines of the tent nearby to the dock. Shivering with fear and suffering from grevious wounds, the small creature was able to gasp just three words before pain and suffering took thier toll... "He is coming...". <BR>	Even the mighty high-elf cleric, a veteran of many battles and a hardened adventurer was unable to save the poor creature's life. Humans, trolls, and elves alike gathered round, for once forgetting there differences. But no matter how they tried, they could no make heads or tails of his last words. What could they mean? Did the short one speak of a mighty hero who was coming to aid those in need? Or of a great storm arise far off on the horizon? AS the others gazed on in wonderment at the now lifeless body, a trio of Iksar Monks stood off to the side and silently scanned the horizon. They could sense a powerful force gathering strength far off among the sands. Before long, a Necromancer, her concentration broken, rose from her tome and turned her eyes towards the dunes as well. A great evil was stirring. One of the monks began to speak, but was immediatly silenced as his Master flung a clawed fist into the air and hissed for silence. Conversation near the tent quieted and all eyes turned towards the scaled one in anticipation. It could be heard, and felt by all now, a steady beat, like the drums of a thousand warriors, reverbrated through the sand at thier feet. As they watched, a great shadow fell upon the dunes as a towering form rose atop the the crest of the nearest one. The form was immense, and in an instant, everyone at the docks knew what the halfling spoke of. <BR>	The two monks backed away in terror from thier Master as he too began to panic. He suddenly turned to the crowd, his eyes wide with fear, "He is here... Cazel!". At that precise moment, the massive form cuaght sight of the large group at the docks, and began to take great strides across the sand, only one word upon his hate-filled mind, destroy! Within an instant, the sand giant was upon them! Flinging aside several trolls as he strode through. The mass of adventurers scattered in panic as Cazel's massive fist, the hand of the gods itself, smashed through the stone pillar nearby. The massive tower crumpled, burying many who hid in it's shadow. He then went on a rampage, the necromancer and her companions were slain as they tried in vain to gate from that horrible place. The giant flung the small shack nearby into a group of fleeing warriors, knocking them about as if they were not more than a few twigs upon the sand.<BR>	Within moments, the slaughter had ended and many heroes lay slain across the beach. One adventurer, however, had lept into the water, and swam far away fromt aht terrible scene. The paladin returned to shore, having shed his armor and weapons in order to escape, and saw the death and destruction that now lay before him. To his right, the giant had once again returned to the dunes and was now seted atop the largest of them, watching the horizon. Knowing this was his only chance, the paladin began to run in the direction of the the Oasis, a great lake were many powerful warlords and socerers kept vigil. Within hours, he reached the shore of the lake that lay at the center of the Oasis, and within moments was met by a pack of wolves. He threw his hands in front of his face to try and protect himself, but the wolves were docile creatures, and with a crackel of supernatural energies, rose to become nine druids. "Oh great and powerful ones!" The paladin stuttered, gasping for air after the long run and attempting to regain his composure, "Please! A great tragedy as take place!" One of the druids, wearing garments that looked to be spun from nature itself stepped forward and kneeled beside him. "Warrior of the church, we have sensed this great evil. Our companions, the plains cats have brought us news of a great and powerful monster of immense strength that has made his home among the dunes. We have sent word to our brethren to the North, and to our time honoured friends, the rangers in the west. They shall soon arrive, with help of thier wizzard friends." The paladin summoned all his strength and rose. "Thank you, but we will need much more to defeat this great evil..." He managed to gasp before collapsing into unconsiousness from fatigue. The druids turned to one another, and resumed thier canine forms. Within moments, they set out for the far reaches of the desert to call upon whomever they could find.<BR>	As night fell, the giant had roamed beyond the dunes to the great encampments of the Orcs. There he stood, the Orcs regarding him with a deep respect, and he looked upon them as brothers in slaughter. Just then, a great flash upon the horizon blinded all who were present for but a moment as groups of Rangers in full battle regalia and thier wizard escorts teleported in nearby. The wizards immeadiatly summoned elementals of earth, fire, water, and air. The Orcs, maddened by the appearance of the large army, set up a ferocious howl and rushed towards the elven ranks.<BR>	Clad in Mithril armour, the elves fitted arrows to thier bowstrings and let volley after volley of deadly missiles fly towards the oncoming wall of green bodies. Many an Orc were slain, but more clambered over thier fallen comrades and rushed on. The rangers, thier arrows depleted, drew thier swords and spears and prepared to do battle. The Wizards were the first to strike, great comets of ice and fire fell from the heavens, decimating the Orcish ranks, but still more came. The two armies met upon the crest of a great dune. The sparkling sands were at once stained with the blood of elves and orcs alike. Swords shone like diamonds in the dark, lit by the moon above. Spears and dagger flashed as they flew about, cutting down thier targets. The Orc ranks held solid, and the battle seemed to be fairly even. The wizards sent in elementals and within moments, the Orc lines were crushed. Sensing victory, the elves began to chase the fleeing orcs down the northern slop of the dune. When all at once, the great Cazel entered the fray, crushing and rending the elven rangers as he ran through. At once,t he tide of battle shifted, and the Elves began to seek cover. The wizards cast fireballs and ice storms upon the great giant, to no avail. Despite this, the battle raged for days all across the desert, the elves steadily losing ground.<BR>	As the battle began to wane,a new force entered the fray. The barbarians of Halas, and the great armies of Kaladim rushed into battle with a howl unlike no other. But the Orcs had help of thier own. Runners had been sent far and wide to alert the evil creatures of the land as to the battle now being fought among the dunes of Ro. Gnolls arrived from the hills of Qeynos, commanded by the powerful Splitpaw. The wall of fur cascaded down the plateau walls and met the barbarina forces headlong. The two armies began a terrific struggle as the Dwarven hordes rushed by, headed for the Orcs and the giant Cazel.<BR>	Within moments, the Dwarves were upon the enemy, and the elves began to fight with renewed vigor. The remaining wizards, their numbers dwindling, put up a terrific fight, freezing, blasting, scorching, and vaporizing the green-skinned Orcs before them. But the battle was lost, the barbarians, unable to hold thier ground against the mighty ranks of the Blackburrow Gnolls, retreated. The Dwarves too, faired miserably. Despite thier fine weapons and immeasurable skill, the Dwarven, Elvish, and Barabarian armies were forced to retreat. Cazel rushed forward and using his great strength, tore throught the fleeing armies.<BR>	Little did the Orcs and Gnolls know, but the bodies of those slain in combat rose up, to  he command of a circle of powerful necromancers. The dark ones floated high above the fray, draining the life force of the Orcs below, as their undead army lurched into combat. Seeing this remarkable change of events, the barbarians bellowed war cries and turned upon Cazel, as did thier compatriots, the Rangers and the Dwarves. Despite being woefully overpowered, the armies of good fought valiantly against the giant of the desert. Seeing this, the necromancers turned and summoned forth a slew of the most feared of all the supernatural beings, the dark and towering Spectres. These great wraiths passed through the battle and on toward the giant. Within moment, they were upon him, casting dark curses and slashing away at him with great magical weapons no mortal being could challenge. The giant, enraged by the swarm of terrifying beings, did not notice the gathering clouds above. <BR>	The dark storm began to rage in the heavens and a torrent of rain began to fall over the battle field. Lightning struck left and right as a group of powerful druids announced thier arrival. The creatures of the forest, summoned by thier masters, rushed across the dunes in a great wave. This monstrous force of nature was instantly upon the enemy. Grizzlies and Dire Wolves crushed the hapless gnolls and orcs as if they were child's playthings.<BR>	The orcs, unable to retreat, had no choice but to turn and fact this new foe. Slowly, the forces of good triumphed. The orc legions lay slain, with few remaining centurions able to fight. At last the battle seemed to draw to a close, with only Cazel remaining. Seeing the odds were against him, Cazel let out a warcry and rushed into the ranks of the Barbarians and Elves. </P><P>**to be continued**</P><P>-~:==&lt;[o]&gt;==:~-<BR>Scaelus Vindictus<BR>-~:==&lt;[o]&gt;==:~-</font></td>
